// Repro from a plain clone (golden case for TestSanitizeIntegration):
//
//	git clone https://github.com/gnolang/gno && cd gno
//	git fetch origin pull/6304/head && git checkout a8bdd53b08e988227136f8b74f4cd6571956e5f4
//	cp <this file> gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown/golden/sanitize/
//	go test ./gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown -run 'TestSanitizeIntegration/b3-lines-removed-reach-catalog-dedent-split-deletes-lrd' -count=1 -v
//
// BlockRich, document level: a fence opened 1 space in (CM 4.5 allows 0-3),
// content at column 0. goldmark alone renders one code block holding all
// three lines, and sanitize.Block still does. closeFencesAtDedent
// (gnovm/stdlibs/chain/markdown/markdown.go) writes a closer before
// `# install`, so the code lines render as markdown: `# install` becomes an
// <h1>, and the bracket walker then deletes `[a]: http://x` as a link
// reference definition. The ADR's fidelity cost says such a line "shows a
// backslash"; here it vanishes from the page.
//
// Sections below pin the head's actual output (the test passes at head).
// Fixed expectation, once the documented cost holds: output.html keeps a
// `\[a]: http://x` (or `[a]: http://x`) line visible instead of dropping it.
// MARKDOWNFUNC: BlockRich
// CONTEXT: REALM BEFORE\n%s\nREALM AFTER
-- input.md --
 ```sh
# install
[a]: http://x
make
 ```
-- output.md --


 ```sh
 ```
# install
make
 ```
 ```

-- output.html --
<p>REALM BEFORE</p>
<pre><code class="language-sh"></code></pre>
<h1>install</h1>
<p>make</p>
<pre><code></code></pre>
<p>REALM AFTER</p>
